# Functors and Morphisms, Chapter 1: Introduction

The source section introduces the relationship between morphisms of schemes
and functors between their categories of quasi-coherent modules.  It also
describes the analogous relationship between a scheme and its category of
quasi-coherent modules, and, for a Noetherian scheme, between the scheme and
its category of coherent modules.

These paragraphs state the scope of the chapter rather than a standalone
definition, theorem, displayed identity or diagram, exact sequence, example,
hypothesis, or mathematically meaningful warning.  The symbols `X`, `Y`,
`QCoh`, and `Coh` occur only in this motivating description; the corresponding
mathematical interfaces belong to the later numbered sections where they are
used.  The bibliographic reference is likewise not mathematical content.
